      "heading": "U3 · Development techniques and solutions",
      "sentence": "Make the idea visible. Learn from the change. Decide what to keep.",
      "quote": "Many doors opened. One fits the brief. Close the rest on purpose. Spring.",
      "quote_origin": "tao_invented",
      "citation": {
        "label": "(Tao of Creativity)",
        "href": "/creativity-techniques-uem/lessons/en/creativity-techniques/u-3-development-solutions/#references"
      }
    },
    {
      "slide_role": "analysis_opener",
      "background_kind": "geometrical",
      "heading": "Analysis opens the class",
      "sentence": "From session 3: two students defend a D1 piece for 15 minutes. Show what changed between versions."
    },
    {
      "slide_role": "analysis_model",
      "background_kind": "profield",
      "media_slot_id": "U3.still.profield-2",
      "heading": "Read the development",
      "sentence": "Name language, medium, and support. Then ask what the next version was trying to learn."
    },
    {
      "slide_role": "masterclass",
      "background_kind": "profield",
      "media_slot_id": "U3.still.profield-3",
      "heading": "1 · Make it rough, make it early",
      "sentence": "A rough prototype is a question in material form. Make the smallest version that can teach you something.",
      "quote": "A rough thing can answer a question that a polished thing hides.",
      "quote_origin": "tao_invented",
      "citation": {
        "label": "(Cross 2006, 17)",
        "href": "/creativity-techniques-uem/lessons/en/creativity-techniques/u-3-development-solutions/#ref-cross-2006"
      }
    },
    {
      "slide_role": "masterclass",
      "background_kind": "profield",
      "media_slot_id": "U3.still.profield-4",
      "heading": "2 · Defer judgement",
      "sentence": "Protect a short space for variation before you decide what works. Then judge with a named criterion."
    },
    {
      "slide_role": "masterclass",
      "background_kind": "profield",
      "media_slot_id": "U3.still.profield-5",
      "heading": "3 · Iterate with an exit",
      "sentence": "Write the test before the next version. Stop when the test is answered."
    },
    {
      "slide_role": "masterclass",
      "background_kind": "profield",
      "media_slot_id": "U3.still.profield-6",
      "heading": "4 · Sketch to think",
      "sentence": "Three quick arrangements can show relationships that one polished drawing hides.",
      "quote": "Sketching enables exploration of the problem space and the solution space to proceed together.",
      "quote_origin": "page_verified",
      "citation": {
        "label": "(Cross 2006, 46)",
        "href": "/creativity-techniques-uem/lessons/en/creativity-techniques/u-3-development-solutions/#ref-cross-2006"
      }
    },
    {
      "slide_role": "masterclass",
      "background_kind": "profield",
      "media_slot_id": "U3.still.profield-1",
      "heading": "5 · Open the solution space",
      "sentence": "Reframe an unclear brief as two or three questions. Make one small response to each.",
      "citation": {
        "label": "(Beghetto and Karwowski 2025, 1)",
        "href": "/creativity-techniques-uem/lessons/en/creativity-techniques/u-3-development-solutions/#ref-beghetto-karwowski-2025"
      }
    },
    {
      "slide_role": "masterclass",
      "background_kind": "profield",
      "media_slot_id": "U3.still.profield-2",
      "heading": "6 · Reflect at checkpoints",
      "sentence": "Write what changed, what stayed, and what the change taught you."
    },
